WEBVTT

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.330
I didn't think I'd ever be able to play that piece again.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.330
Just like Paganini was there for Liszt...

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:14.030
I guess you could say that you are there as my violinist.

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:56.130
A Heartful Harmony

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:07.660
Tsukimori-kun.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:14.870
What is it?

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:16.160
I was waiting for you.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:18.200
For me?

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:22.110
Here, take this.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.000
What is it?

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.340
Tsukimori-kun, isn't this...

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:38.630
I'll be performing with my mother.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:40.800
With your mother?

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:45.010
Or maybe... You're nervous because your parents are coming?

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:49.760
No way, did I just hit the nail on the head?

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:56.610
It seems like Tsukimori-kun only ever gets nervous when he performs in front of his parents.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.470
I want you to hear it.

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:03.070
Tsukimori-kun.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:11.650
Could it be that Tsukimori-kun is trying to get over that barrier?

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:16.900
Thank you. I'll definitely come.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.220
Later.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.860
I'll do my best, too.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.420
You're really into it, Kahoko Hino.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:43.520
Reading the score?

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:45.290
Yeah.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:48.450
I was thinking that following the score is the fundamental first step, you know.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:53.810
The composer put all their feelings and intentions into the score, after all.

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:57.790
So I was thinking if I could just get that to come through a little...

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:01.430
Well, it's good to go back to the source.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:03.630
But, you know...

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:07.600
Lili?

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:12.220
You're the person playing the violin, and no one else.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:13.400
Right...

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:14.910
That's true, isn't it?

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:20.930
That's all I wanted to say. Good luck!

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:24.850
Lili?

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.140
Thank you! I got some good shots.

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:35.330
Oh, no... It was nothing.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:39.820
The final selection is almost here. Good luck!

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:42.550
Yes. Thank you very much.

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:48.100
You know, Fuyuumi-chan, you seem to have a bit more self-confidence than before.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:51.490
I wonder if you've matured a bit because of the competition?

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.200
I've matured?

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.190
No way! I'm still...

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:00.080
You don't have to deny it so strongly.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:03.620
No, I've really just got such a long way to go.

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:07.320
If we're talking about a long way to go, we should be worried more about Hino-chan.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:10.560
Although she's gotten a bit better lately.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.790
Oh, it's Fuyuumi-san!

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:17.630
It's almost time for the final selection, right?

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:20.330
We'll be cheering for you, so do your best!

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.460
Uh, OK!

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:27.540
Thank you... very... much...

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:32.470
I guess you really do have a long way to go on this front.

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:50.990
Sensei, are you OK?

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:55.280
Hino? Don't sneak up on me like that.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:58.790
Sorry, I was just returning the music stand.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:02.500
Oh, the music stand. Just leave it over there.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:03.510
Sure.

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:11.030
You won't keep singing?

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:18.810
That cassette tape from before was you, Kanazawa-sensei, right?

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.440
You had a really wonderful singing voice.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:31.660
Kanazawa-sensei has been looking like that recently.

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:36.160
Could it be that Kanazawa-sensei's throat...

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:41.040
If you leave without finding a new door opened for you, it'll be difficult for you.

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:44.880
I...

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.420
I'm sorry!

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:50.980
You...

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:59.060
Whenever I watch you all trying so hard, my wounds heal.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:06.480
Just sayin'.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:13.990
One day, I really want to hear you sing, Sensei.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:15.740
Pardon me!

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.560
Hihara-sempai, how long have you been there?

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:15.030
Just for a bit. I was waiting for you to finish practicing.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:22.860
Um, Hihara-sempai?

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:25.390
This is a reward for all your hard work, Kaho-chan!

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:28.870
Sweet things help keep your energy up.

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:31.450
Well, that's what Yunoki always told me, anyway.

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:33.240
Yunoki-sempai?

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:36.490
I wonder what he's doing about now?

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.480
This is great!

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:42.830
Here, you try some, Kaho-chan!

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.150
Sure, thanks.

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:49.420
It's delicious!

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:51.920
Really? Thank goodness!

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:54.350
Yes, it really is.

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:01.470
Hihara-sempai?

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:06.900
Oh, nothing... It's just like this is a guy's dream, you know...

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.610
A guy's dream?

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:11.780
Yeah, you know... Eating cake with a girl he li-

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:16.700
I-I mean, eating a cake he likes with a girl!

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:21.790
Speaking of which, what kind of music do you like?

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:25.580
What kind of music?

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:33.130
Wh-What am I saying?

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.070
I like the Gavotte, I guess...

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:38.800
It's cute, and it really resonates with my heart.

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:42.470
Gavotte?

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:58.360
I'm performing for those important to me at the final selection.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:06.080
For the people that have been cheering me on, and gave me the energy...

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.080
I'm going to continue on with music.

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.210
Hihara-sempai...

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:14.710
I just wanted to say that to you, Kaho-chan.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.990
Let's do our best together.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:27.650
What do you think?

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:30.390
Yes, you've definitely improved.

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:34.090
But I still have a lot of work to do on my expression.

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:35.780
That's true.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.960
But you're really starting to get it solidly.

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:41.000
Really?

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:46.290
You don't sound unsure of yourself like you did before.

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:50.750
I wonder if it's because I'm trying to play it like the score says.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:53.960
That's right! The basics are important, after all.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:57.060
OK then, shall we go again from the top?

00:10:57.060 --> 00:10:57.700
Sure.

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:03.470
This part is tricky.

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:07.230
Once more, just like the score says...

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:08.600
But that's...

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.540
... not like you, Sempai.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:18.290
Shimizu-kun! But didn't you say "just like the score" before yourself?

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:22.740
But that isn't your score, Sempai.

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:26.220
Yes, it is.

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:33.670
Your score is in here.

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:43.060
I finally found my own score.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:46.930
Thanks to you, Sempai.

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:51.030
Thank you very much.

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:57.040
Shimizu-kun...

00:12:15.590 --> 00:12:17.800
I guess I got here a little too early.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:40.990
Tsukimori-kun.

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:45.720
Tsukimori-kun!

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:47.580
Hino?

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:53.010
Thank you for inviting me today.

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:53.770
No problem.

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:57.500
Is there something...

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:02.300
I didn't expect you to be in a place like this before you perform, Tsukimori-kun.

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:05.470
Tsukimori-kun?

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:10.050
That's true. I don't ever act like this.

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:14.270
But today I just wanted to feel the wind for some reason.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:20.960
Um...

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:26.720
Ah, cute!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.070
Pink shells break easily.

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:35.360
What'll you do if you hurt your fingers again?

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:39.880
There is music that can only be born from those fingers.

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:42.150
Please cherish them more.

00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:44.170
Tsukimori-kun.

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:52.650
Thank you. I'll be careful.

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:59.360
It's really pretty.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:04.430
I want to touch all kinds of things, feel them, experience them...

00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:10.490
Even if I get hurt, I want to express that pain through my music as well.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:12.650
I see.

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:18.250
Your music sparkles from all the experiences in your heart.

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:22.000
It's born from the bottom of your heart.

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:25.180
So that's your music, I see.

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:31.780
You're the person playing the violin, and no one else.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:36.690
Your score is in here.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:41.660
My... music...

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:52.410
I feel a lot better now.

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:56.240
I think I can give a good performance now.

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:02.660
Oh, Kaho-chan!

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:05.990
So you got a ticket, too.

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:07.140
Y-Yes.

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:13.250
I was really surprised to get a letter from Tsukimori-kun's mom just like that.

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:15.770
From his mom?

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:17.470
Oh, you're early.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:22.080
So you also got a ticket from Tsukimori-kun's mom?

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:26.800
Yeah, I didn't think I'd get a letter from Misa Hamai herself.

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:28.990
Which means...

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:31.450
It's over here, Shimizu-kun.

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:37.570
Fuyuumi-chan and Shimizu-kun, you also got tickets.

00:15:37.570 --> 00:15:38.740
Yes.

00:15:38.740 --> 00:15:42.490
I met Shimizu-kun outside of the hall.

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:45.000
So all of you are here, then?

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:50.640
Then I'm the only one to get a ticket from Tsukimori-kun?

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:54.930
But then, why is Kaho-chan the only one in a different row?

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.520
Wh-Who knows?

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:50.410
It's finally Tsukimori-kun's turn.

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:14.890
Tsukimori-sempai's performance today was really wonderful.

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:17.590
His playing was just all sparkly, you know?

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:19.780
Sparkly?

00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:22.560
That really doesn't suit him.

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:24.460
It was a lot of fun, don't you think?

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:29.470
Yeah! If his usual performance is like a perfectly tailored suit,

00:19:29.470 --> 00:19:32.440
then today's was like he loosened his necktie a bit, you know?

00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:36.900
It was easy going, and affectionate...

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:38.920
Yes, that's right.

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:46.040
Kanon-san, thank you so much for your wonderful singing today.

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:47.830
No, I should thank you.

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:52.540
It is a great honor to be able to stand on the same stage as you, Hamai-san.

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:55.960
Same here. I hope we can get to do this again sometime.

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:56.840
As do I.

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:11.060
Everyone, thank you for coming.

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:17.190
N-No, it's us who should be thankful... for you... inviting us...

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:19.320
It was REALLY fun!

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:22.450
Well I'm glad to hear that.

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:29.600
As I thought.

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:36.790
It's almost time for the final selection. Everyone, do your best.

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:37.690
Yes, ma'am!

00:20:41.240 --> 00:20:43.570
That was a good concert!

00:20:43.570 --> 00:20:47.470
I'm looking forward to your performance for the final selection, Tsukimori-kun.

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:49.100
Thank you very much.

00:20:49.340 --> 00:20:52.600
Hihara-sempai, you seem relaxed.

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:55.470
Well, relaxed...

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:57.520
After all, it's the last one.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:21:00.750
So I've got to give it my all, so I have no regrets!

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:02.360
Right, Kaho-chan?

00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:03.690
Right!

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:15.900
I've decided to perform in my own way for the final selection.

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:20.880
Regardless of what the score says, I'll just perform the music that's inside of me.

00:21:22.040 --> 00:21:26.160
I'm looking forward to your performance, Kaho-sempai.

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:28.280
Thank you, Fuyuumi-chan!

00:21:29.380 --> 00:21:34.550
No fair, Fuyuumi-chan! I wanted to say that first!

00:21:34.550 --> 00:21:37.180
Fuyuumi-chan, doesn't that shop look cute over there?

00:21:37.180 --> 00:21:39.230
Want to go eat some cake?

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:40.200
Sure.

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:44.950
I guess that's how Kaho-chan always is, you know?

00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:53.020
I wonder if we'll always be trying to catch up to her.

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:39.730
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:48.130
Along with Bach and Beethoven, Brahms is known as one of the three great "B"s of German music.

00:23:48.130 --> 00:23:56.240
His first symphony is a magnificent work, but it took him over 20 years to complete!

00:23:56.710 --> 00:23:58.510
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:58.510 --> 00:24:03.290
After this composer passed away, Brahms devoted himself to his widow and family.

00:24:03.290 --> 00:24:05.040
Who was that composer?

00:24:05.760 --> 00:24:08.100
It's finally the final selection.

00:24:08.100 --> 00:24:13.050
I'm going to perform with all my heart for everyone that has supported me all this time.

00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:14.740
Please listen.

00:24:15.310 --> 00:24:17.930
Next episode: My Beloved Ave Maria.

00:24:17.930 --> 00:24:19.420
It's the final episode.

00:24:20.390 --> 00:24:23.910
The answer is... Schumann!
